  {
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Currently I don\u2019t think there is a plan for supporting 128 bit integer types. The cost to extend the type matrix is very high due to compile time, and there are a lot of places where 64 bit integers are the maximum width we could support for computation without significant changes to the library\u2019s internals.\r\n\r\nHow is your input data being stored / computed? (Where do the 128 bit types come from?) Do you need this for cuDF Python or some other interface?",
    "created_at": "2023-02-07T13:34:31Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/rapidsai/cudf/issues/12716#issuecomment-1420784733",
